{"ts": "2026-11-04T19:58:43.409502Z", "run_id": "r-20261104T1958Z-2455", "unit": "openspec:add-crash-harness", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-002", "target": "C-0f1c4174", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The criterion is satisfied as written. validateOptions runs before any directory, log or child exists and names scenario, faultPoints, args and readyTimeoutMs with the bounds the scenario gives; the child writes one stderr line and exits 1 for scenario_failed, scenario_not_ready, scenario_invalid and scenario_unloadable, the parent keeps the last non-empty stderr line and the exit code in CRASH_START_FAILED, a ready timeout SIGKILLs the child and rejects with reason timeout and the dead pid, and READY_TIMEOUT_MS is 30000. The two tracing tests assert every clause of the scenario, including the five failure lines, the exit codes 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, the dead timed-out pid and the absent engine.log, and both passed. The judge's fail came only from an unexecuted counterexample about non-plain args objects, which this scenario does not pin down.", "text_sha256": "9f73df485d661de87ebf560b2791369ea8e3401d15d412ce5a234086588d6bf1", "answer_sha256": "5e8fe73ac2802e2a0d34c9d27d946accf6492652039f033de9b853ba09bc554b", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-04T19:58:43.410727Z", "run_id": "r-20261104T1958Z-2455", "unit": "openspec:add-crash-harness", "seq": 6, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-003", "target": "F-2c3fda0e", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is waived. The args option is typed Readonly<Record<string, string>> on a test-only harness, so a Date or class instance reaches validateOptions only through an explicit cast in test code. The validation refuses a non-object, null, an array and any non-string own value, which is what the specification's scenario pins down with args { a: 1 }; an object with string own fields is copied correctly, and the child re-validates the payload. An empty args from a Date has no effect on production code, no security impact and no scenario that it breaks, so a fix unit is not warranted.", "text_sha256": "3e2dcebb2eef3d9d2dd469281ebb72efdb2803051452abb93132c04163ac1ec1", "answer_sha256": "a6132466862f2442f2019bd47aa608c5edc073301699488ea9f3c0beed9da7cd", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-04T19:58:43.411557Z", "run_id": "r-20261104T1958Z-2455", "unit": "openspec:add-crash-harness", "seq": 7, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "F-fb0ff054", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is waived. Part names are the key of the e2e stack's handle map by contract: PartContext.handles is a ReadonlyMap keyed by name and parts find each other through it, so two parts with one name are unsupported everywhere in the stack. Both discoverParts and the part registry reject a duplicate name with STACK_PART_DUPLICATE before startCrashCluster sees the list, and withDedicatedCluster passes only the discovered list. startCrashCluster stores and closes handles exactly as startE2eStack does, which design decision 5 asks for. No scenario pins the duplicate-name case, and a test handing in two same-named fakes would be misusing the part model, not exposing a defect of this unit.", "text_sha256": "6e035cbc680da8507caaafba1a23c304935816d20adc7d1bf0c2e78f2280562b", "answer_sha256": "d70c24204551f6ce5665ed0c986f6514d5bfd6a4e2a76235915eb42f350a4491", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
